{"id": "EUVD-2026-32453", "enisaUuid": "61046770-164a-34ea-b4ad-b7d0c5e4a4f2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: nSVM: Avoid clearing VMCB_LBR in vmcb12\n\nsvm_copy_lbrs() always marks VMCB_LBR dirty in the destination VMCB.\nHowever, nested_svm_vmexit() uses it to copy LBRs to vmcb12, and\nclearing clean bits in vmcb12 is not architecturally defined.\n\nMove vmcb_mark_dirty() to callers and drop it for vmcb12.\n\nThis also facilitates incoming refactoring that does not pass the entire\nVMCB to svm_copy_lbrs().", "datePublished": "2026-05-27T12:57:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:41:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/165b08d2d1346dce5ed43db65e10f3194b9ae2fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11d347b7edf5093d69aca72317300798a32bfd6b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3f0981a5a0e0bd51ad74cc7d9eed32294b24002", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9efe23568806d1cd06f7d146f9b3037b8d585a9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b53ab5167a81537777ac780bbd93d32613aa3bda"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h9fc-vq2v-qf62", "CVE-2026-46071"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17c26228-12ca-3b94-955d-b52ba22748c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.27"}, {"id": "311714c0-ef79-3cc3-9f26-9a5705bbc044", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d20c796ca3709801f8a7fa36e8770a3dd8ebd34e <a3f0981a5a0e0bd51ad74cc7d9eed32294b24002"}, {"id": "41ca4567-c41c-3f62-a521-d2365521cfd2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "4d9d5728-4674-3a30-955b-bad3a88e2634", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "5514770f-9e08-33b3-b77f-52dba77e5f2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "6cf992e8-c3e1-3cd7-afa9-549b46